# Local release signing - the same key EAS holds. Never commit these.
release.jks
keystore.properties

# Signed APKs, staged here to be handed over.
#
# Each one is about 56 MB and a fresh pair is built most days - committing them
# would add that much to the repository every time, permanently, for a file
# nobody ever reads back out of git. GitHub warns above 50 MB and refuses
# above 100.
builds/

# Firebase's Android client config.
#
# It carries a Google API key for this project. The key is a client one and
# ships inside the APK anyway, so it is not a password - but it is still a key
# on Mohan's Google Cloud project, it is only as safe as the restrictions set
# on it in the console, and a public repository is a far easier place to find
# one than a decompiled APK. It stays on the machines that build.
google-services.json
